.SH NAME
isalpha, isupper, islower, isdigit, isxdigit, isalnum, isspace , ispunct, isprint, isgraph, iscntrl, isascii \- character classification 
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <ctype.h>
.PP
.B int isalpha \fR(\fIc\fR)
.br
.B int \fIc\fR;
.PP
.B . . .
.SH DESCRIPTION
These macros classify \s-1ASCII\s0-coded integer values
by table lookup.
Each is a predicate returning nonzero for true,
zero for false.
.B Isascii\^
is defined on all integer values; the rest
are defined only where 
.B isascii\^
is true and on the single non-\s-1ASCII\s0 value
.SM
.B EOF
(see
.BR stdio (3)).
.TP 15n
.B isalpha\^
.I c\^
is a letter
.TP
.B isupper\^
.I c\^
is an upper case letter
.TP
.B islower\^
.I c\^
is a lower case letter
.TP
.B isdigit\^
.I c\^
is a digit [0-9]
.TP
.B isxdigit\^
.I c\^
is a hexidecimal digit [0-9], [A-F] or [a-f]
.TP
.B isalnum\^
.I c\^
is an alphanumeric
.TP
.B isspace\^
.I c\^
is a space, tab, carriage return, new-line, vertical tab, or form-feed
.TP
.B ispunct\^
.I c\^
is a punctuation character (neither control nor alphanumeric)
.TP
.B isprint\^
.I c\^
is a printing character, code 040 (space) through 0176 (tilde)
.TP
.B isgraph\^
.I c\^
is a printing character, like
.B isprint\^
except false for space
.TP
.B iscntrl\^
.I c\^
is a delete character (0177) or ordinary control character
(less than 040).
.TP
.B isascii\^
.I c\^
is an \s-1ASCII\s0 character, code less than 0200
.SH SEE ALSO
ascii(7).
